//@version=5
// NON-VACUITY CONTROL FOR THE RENDER GATE -- this script MUST NOT draw.
// Every bar of its column is 0/0, so the column holds no finite value,
// `planBindings` gives the plot no series, and `legendChips` stamps the chip
// `data-computed="false"`. It is inside the lookback budget on purpose: the
// long-window control (ctrl-01) never reaches the chart because the product
// refuses it at Save, so it can prove nothing about the RENDER gate.
// If the harness calls this CHART_RENDERABLE, `drewNothing` is not discriminating
// and every CHART_RENDERABLE it has ever printed is unearned.
indicator("Control Non Finite Column", overlay = false)
zero = close - close
plot(close / zero, title = "Empty", color = color.purple, linewidth = 2)
